  "selection_rule": "Run control_plane/research_control_bootstrap.py before any canonical runtime view, then run research_control_dispatch.py as the canonical control-plane route. The bootstrap locally isolates only exact-pinned publication forks, invalid current task publications, nonoperational Driver-review provenance, and follow-up authority derived solely from those reviews; it selects no replacement authority and leaves unrelated tasks untouched. The router then first preserves/adopts any owner scope whose valid CLAIM is independently observed stale, without creating a second CLAIM. If no stale-recoverable owner is observed, it delegates ordinary fresh task selection to tools/research_dispatch.py and active-cohort lane selection to tools/research_lane_dispatch.py. If both fresh selectors are empty but any valid owner lease has unknown conversation liveness, the result is VERIFY_SESSION_LIVENESS rather than NO_DISPATCH. For ordinary fresh tasks, historical state/priority/leverage/staleness ordering remains unchanged; AWAITING_REVIEW and COMPLETE are never selected. When an ACTIVE cohort exists, canonical task status is projected to COHORT_ACTIVE and task-global ownership is disabled. Live events must come from raw server-authenticated Issue #240 comments whose exact server actor is authorized. Compatible historical execution records may supply the same durable binding but cannot replace the live winning claim requirement.",
  "interaction_budget": "Recovery routing reuses existing owner state and ephemeral liveness evidence. Fault isolation is local deterministic repository-state reduction with no periodic polling and no extra CLAIM. Authentication and actor authorization reuse the same Issue #240 comments already needed for semantic control events. Ordinary tasks add no new periodic poll; a liveness verification is required only when fresh dispatch is empty and a valid owner lease would otherwise cause a false NO_DISPATCH, or when stale adoption is being considered."
